# nwg-displays

nwg-displays 0.5.0, the display layout app that the app launcher's Displays Settings entry starts (the desktop package's `@DISTRO_ID@-launch-monitors`): roadmap step 6. nwg-displays is a Python 3 program (GTK 3 through PyGObject, the `gtk-layer-shell` library for its overlay windows, and `i3ipc` to talk to the compositor's socket) that shows the connected monitors as boxes you drag around, and on Apply writes the layout, resolution, refresh rate, scale and transform of each monitor to a configuration file the compositor reads. Ubuntu's archive carries 0.3.28, which writes only Hyprland's old `monitors.conf` format; Hyprland 0.55 and newer, which Omarchy @OMARCHY_TAG@ builds on, read a Lua configuration, and nwg-displays writes that Lua file since 0.4.3. See `docs/0 - plan.md`, "System settings UI".

The package keeps the upstream name, as the policy says for third-party software we package from source, and the version `0.5.0-0oaxaca1`: a new upstream release on Debian's packaging, so the `-0oaxaca1` revision marks "not in Debian yet", sorts above the archive's `0.3.28-1`, and sorts below a future Debian `0.5.0-1`.

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `debian/` | Debian's `nwg-displays` 0.3.28-1 packaging (Debian Python Team, uploader Maytham Alsudany), with our changelog entry and Maintainer |
| `upstream` | the upstream tarball's URL and SHA-256; `scripts/build.sh` downloads the tarball as the orig tarball and unpacks the tarball around `debian/` before `dpkg-source` |

Unlike the `@DISTRO_ID@-*` packages, this directory holds no upstream source: `make build PKG=packages/nwg-displays` fetches the source into `build/`.

## What the package installs

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `/usr/bin/nwg-displays` | the GUI; the entry point `nwg_displays.main:main` from upstream's `setup.py` |
| `/usr/bin/nwg-displays-apply` | a command that applies a saved profile without opening the GUI (`nwg_displays.scripts.apply_profile_json:main`) |
| `/usr/bin/nwg-displays-toggle-wallpapers` | a command that toggles the wallpapers a profile stores (`nwg_displays.scripts.toggle_profile_wallpapers:main`) |
| `/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/nwg_displays/` | the Python module: `main.py`, `tools.py`, `profiles.py`, `settings_applier/`, `wallpaper_manager/`, `scripts/`, the Glade UI file and CSS under `resources/`, translations under `langs/` |
| `/usr/share/applications/nwg-displays.desktop`, `/usr/share/pixmaps/nwg-displays.svg` | the menu entry and its icon, from Debian's `debian/nwg-displays.install` |
| `/usr/share/doc/nwg-displays/README.md` | upstream's README, from Debian's `debian/nwg-displays.docs` |

## Where the packaging and the source come from

| Path in `packages/nwg-displays/` | Origin | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `debian/rules`, `copyright`, `nwg-displays.install`, `nwg-displays.docs`, `source/format`, `source/options`, `upstream/metadata`, `watch` | Debian's `nwg-displays` 0.3.28-1, fetched from `deb.debian.org` as `nwg-displays_0.3.28-1.debian.tar.xz` on 2026-10-10 (SHA-256 `3b79a6cf...7d52f31`, the one Debian's `.dsc` records) | unchanged. `rules` is `dh $@ --buildsystem=pybuild` with `PYBUILD_NAME=nwg-displays`: pybuild runs upstream's `setup.py` and dh-python fills `${python3:Depends}`. Debian's `gbp.conf` and `salsa-ci.yml` are not copied: those two files drive Debian's own workflow. Debian's `patches/` directory is empty and is not copied |
| `debian/control.in` | Debian's `control` | our `Maintainer`, Debian's as `XSBC-Original-Maintainer` (Ubuntu's convention for a Debian package it changes); the `Vcs-*` fields that named Debian's git tree are dropped. Debian's `Uploaders`, Section, dependencies and Description stay as they are |
| `debian/changelog.in` | ours on top of Debian's history | the `0.5.0-0oaxaca1` and `0.4.4-0oaxaca1` entries with the reasons, then Debian's four entries |
| `debian/patches/hyprland-use-given-paths.patch`, `series` | ours | on Hyprland, creates the monitor and workspace files at the `-m` and `-w` paths, and reads mirrors and the workspaces window from those paths, where 0.5.0 always uses `~/.config/hypr/monitors.conf` and `workspaces.conf`; section "What was checked in the 0.5.0 source" |
| `upstream` | ours | `URL=` of GitHub's tarball for the release tag `v0.5.0` (published 2026-10-20, the newest release on 2026-10-22, checked with `gh api repos/nwg-piotr/nwg-displays/releases`) and `SHA256=` computed from the download on 2026-10-22. GitHub's tag tarball is the same source Debian uses: the `v0.3.28` tag tarball's SHA-256 equals the `nwg-displays_0.3.28.orig.tar.gz` checksum in Debian's `.dsc` (`35ffe993...fad26e9`) |
| `README.md.in` | ours | this summary |

## What was checked in the 0.5.0 source

Each fact names the file in the unpacked `v0.5.0` tarball and the line that proves the fact, as read on 2026-10-22. The 0.4.4 package, `0.4.4-0oaxaca1`, was checked the same way on 2026-10-10.

- **Dependencies.** The set of modules the Python code imports in 0.5.0 is the set of 0.3.28 and 0.4.4 plus the standard library's `re` (`grep -rh '^import\|^from' nwg_displays/` on the trees, compared): `gi` with `Gtk` 3.0, `Gdk` 3.0 and `GtkLayerShell` 0.1 (`nwg_displays/main.py` lines 26, 28 and 39; `nwg_displays/tools.py` lines 13 and 14), `i3ipc`, and the standard library. `importlib_metadata` in `nwg_displays/__about__.py` line 4 is only the fallback when `importlib.metadata` is missing, and Python 3.14 has that module. Upstream's `setup.py` (line 22) declares `install_requires=[]`, so pybuild adds nothing. Debian's `Depends` (`gir1.2-gtk-3.0`, `gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1`, `python3-gi`, `python3-i3ipc`, plus `${python3:Depends}`) therefore stays, and every name is in `stonking` (the versions sbuild installed for the 0.5.0 build on 2026-10-22): `python3-gi` 3.57.1-1, `gir1.2-gtk-3.0` 3.24.52-0ubuntu1, `gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1` 0.10.1-1, `python3-i3ipc` 2.2.1-4 (all `universe` except `python3-gi` and `gir1.2-gtk-3.0` in `main`); the build dependency `dh-sequence-python3` is provided by `dh-python` 7.20260623ubuntu2 and `python3-setuptools` is 78.1.1-0.1build1. The `setup.py` diff between 0.3.28 and 0.4.4 changes only `version=` and adds `scripts/*`, `settings_applier/*` and `wallpaper_manager/*` to `package_data`; between 0.4.4 and 0.5.0 it changes only `version=`. 0.5.0's mangowm support runs `wlr-randr` (`tools.py` line 129), only while `MANGO_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE` is set (`tools.py` lines 487 and 664), so the package does not depend on `wlr-randr`.
- **Lua output for Hyprland 0.55 and newer exists.** `nwg_displays/settings_applier/settings_applier.py`: the GUI's Apply path `_apply_hyprland_gui` builds one `hl.monitor({...})` block per monitor (line 669) and writes the list with `save_list_to_text_file(lines_lua, outputs_path_lua)` (line 688), after it writes the old-format `monitors.conf` lines to the `-m` path (line 687); the profile loader `_apply_hyprland_json` does the same at lines 147 and 158. Workspace rules go to `hl.workspace_rule({...})` blocks in `nwg_displays/main.py` line 1083. The 0.3.28 tree contains no Lua code at all (`grep -ri lua nwg_displays/` finds nothing), and upstream's release note for v0.4.3 says the version "generates `~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua` and `~/.config/hypr/workspaces.lua` for Hyprland v0.55.x". v0.4.4's release note adds Hyprland colour management (`cm`, `sdrbrightness`, `sdrsaturation`, `bitdepth`) and VRR (`vrr`) fields to the same blocks (0.5.0's `settings_applier.py` lines 636 to 656) and fixes monitor descriptions containing `#` in the Lua output.
- **Which file the Lua output goes to by default.** With no option, `-m/--monitors_path` defaults to `<config home>/hypr/monitors.conf` (`nwg_displays/main.py` lines 1252 to 1260; `hypr_config_dir` is `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypr` or `~/.config/hypr`, `main.py` line 70 and `tools.py` lines 24 to 26). The Lua path is derived from the `-m` value: `outputs_path.removesuffix(".conf") + ".lua"` when the value ends in `.conf`, else the fixed string `"~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua"` (`settings_applier.py` lines 675 to 679 and 149 to 153). So the default writes `~/.config/hypr/monitors.conf` and `~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua`, the same file name Omarchy's hand-edited monitor file uses.
- **`-m/--monitors_path` exists and keeps Lua output at a custom path, with one rule.** The option is defined at `main.py` lines 1252 to 1260 and stored as `outputs_path` at line 1339. Because the Lua path is the `.conf` path with the suffix swapped (the lines above), `nwg-displays -m ~/.config/hypr/monitors-gui.conf` writes `monitors-gui.conf` and `monitors-gui.lua` in that directory. A value that does not end in `.conf`, such as the plan's `-m ~/.config/hypr/monitors-gui.lua`, sends the Lua output to the literal string `~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua`, and `save_list_to_text_file` (`tools.py` line 773) opens that string as given, with no tilde expansion, so the write fails. `@DISTRO_ID@-launch-monitors` must pass a `.conf` path and the Lua file to `require()` from Omarchy's `monitors.lua` is then `monitors-gui`.
- **Three places ignore `-m` and `-w`, patched by `hyprland-use-given-paths.patch`.** `nwg_displays/main.py` lines 101 and 102 create `monitors.conf` and `workspaces.conf` in `hypr_config_dir`, empty, while the module is imported, before `main()` parses the options; `tools.py` line 415, in `list_outputs()`, reads mirror lines from `hypr_config_dir/monitors.conf`; `main.py` line 963, in `create_workspaces_window_hypr`, loads the workspaces window from `hypr_config_dir/workspaces.conf`. Saving uses the options (`settings_applier.py` line 687 writes the `.conf` lines to `outputs_path`; `main.py` lines 1050 and 1053 write workspaces to `workspaces_path`), so started as `@DISTRO_ID@-launch-monitors` starts it, unpatched nwg-displays leaves two empty files under `~/.config/hypr`, sees no mirror it has saved and opens the workspaces window empty. 0.4.4 had the same three places (`main.py` lines 85, 86 and 872, `tools.py` line 275). The patch creates the files at the `-m` and `-w` paths after the options are parsed and passes those paths to the other two places. Tested on 2026-10-22 by running the unpatched and patched 0.5.0 trees with `gi` and `i3ipc` replaced by stand-in modules and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` pointing to a scratch folder: unpatched, the folder got `monitors.conf` and `workspaces.conf`, the mirror check read `monitors.conf` and the workspaces window loaded nothing from a `workspaces-gui.conf` holding two rules; patched, the folder got `monitors-gui.conf` and `workspaces-gui.conf`, the mirror check read `monitors-gui.conf` and the window loaded `{1: 'DP-1', 2: 'eDP-1'}`.
- **Files Debian's `install` and `docs` name still exist.** `nwg-displays.desktop`, `nwg-displays.svg` and `README.md` sit at the top of the 0.5.0 tree. Upstream's own `install.sh` installs the same two files to `/usr/share/applications` and `/usr/share/pixmaps`.
- **The source tree carries three dangling symlinks** under `.direnv/` (`flake-profile`, `flake-profile-6-link`, `flake-profile-9-link`), left in the tag by upstream's Nix development shell; the 0.3.28 tarball Debian built from and the 0.4.4 tarball have the same three. They stay in the orig tarball and the build does not touch them.

## Version reasoning

The policy's "third-party we package from source" row gives `<upstream>-0oaxaca<N>`, so `0.4.4-0oaxaca1`, and `0.5.0-0oaxaca1` for the 0.5.0 release. Rejected: the "rebuild from a Debian source package" form `0.3.28-1oaxaca1`, because Debian's source is 0.3.28 and the whole point is the newer upstream, and a native version `0.4.4`, which would hide that Debian's packaging is reused and would not sort below Debian's own `0.4.4-1` when Debian ships that release, at which point the plan says to backport Debian's package instead.
